{
 "_readme": "Hand-written questions for lib/knowledge.js, labelled with the entry that should answer (null = nothing should answer, the assistant must say it does not know). \"dev\" was used while the answers and patterns were written. \"heldout\" was written separately and run once BEFORE any pattern was changed to fit it; the first-pass result is recorded in docs/BENCHMARKS.md. Both are written by the author of the matcher, so they are optimistic: they measure coverage and false-answer behaviour on realistic phrasings, not accuracy on strangers. Real questions will be added from the S0 collection. \"fresh\" was written after the patterns were tuned on dev and heldout, in a different style (spoken fillers, typos, Hinglish, more out-of-scope questions), and run exactly once; its first-pass result is the generalisation figure. \"probe\" holds what an adversarial run against the live assistant turned up (prompt injection, pressure to say \"safe\", markup, Devanagari, \"is this message safe?\"); it was written after those failures and is a regression guard, not a measurement.",
